    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d510">

                <pb facs="0582" n="470" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg470"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Brazilian
                        Chargé.</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d510-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-06-10"><hi rendition="#italic">June 10,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Chargé d’Affaires</hi>: I beg to inclose
                    for your information a copy of an aide-mémoire<anchor n="2" xml:id="d510-f2"/>
                    which was handed to the chargé d’affaires ad interim of Chile on the 1st instant
                    and a copy of an aide-mémoire,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d510-f3"/> which was
                    addressed to the diplomatic representatives of Ecuador and Peru at this capital
                    on the same day, in reference to the mediation between Peru and Ecuador for the
                    settlement of their differences in connection with the arbitration of their
                    conflicting boundary claims.</p>
                <p>These aides-mémoire have been communicated by cable to the American embassy at
                    Petropolis, for communication to your Government.</p>
                <p>I am, my dear Mr. de Lima, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
